# Normalize line endings in the repository so that the index is the single
# source of truth. Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows makes the
# working tree CRLF while the index stays LF, which produces a
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every `git add` and lets individual
# files drift into mixed endings.
#
# Setting `eol=lf` explicitly also overrides that heuristic, so the warning
# stops entirely.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows and MSVC are checked out with CRLF regardless; this repo contains no
# native build inputs, so keep the rule uniform.